  "query_preview": "..\n(Wednesday through next Monday)\nIssued at 1025 PM CDT Sun Oct 11 2026\n\nThe warm and dry weather will continue in the extended period as the \nupper ridging remains. We'll may see some record highs fall \nTuesday through Thursday. The records at Nashville are 88, 89, and\n89 respectively. At Crossville, the records are 82, 81, and 79. \nWe'll get back closer to normal on Friday as shortwave swings \nthrough the Great Lakes which will drag a cold front through our \narea. The moisture with the frontal passage looks meager, so I'm \nnot expecting much in the way of rain with it. Next weekend looks \nlike real Fall with some temperatures in the 30s showing up in the\nmornings.",
